Package: jmpread
Type: Package
Title: Read 'JMP' Binary Data Tables in Native R
Version: 0.0.2
Authors@R: c(
    person("Joseph", "Hill", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "joe@sixhillsgroup.com.au"),
    person("Andy", "Bardagjy", role = "cph",
           comment = "jumpio algorithms adapted under the MIT license"),
    person("Jaakko", "Ruohio", role = "cph",
           comment = "JMPReader.jl format work and MIT-licensed fixtures"))
Description: An experimental reader for 'JMP' binary data tables, implemented
    entirely in R. Supports common numeric, character, temporal and row-state
    column encodings, including gzip compression. Returns data frames with
    source metadata and reports unsupported or malformed encodings. Based
    on binary format work in 'jumpio' <https://github.com/abardagjy/jumpio>
    and 'JMPReader.jl' <https://github.com/jaakkor2/JMPReader.jl>.
    No 'JMP' installation or 'Python' runtime is required.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Suggests: knitr
VignetteBuilder: knitr
URL: https://github.com/JosephHill04/jmpread
BugReports: https://github.com/JosephHill04/jmpread/issues
